# Build-time configuration for production and native builds.
#
# These are committed deliberately. Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_*, meaning they are
# inlined into the client bundle and ship inside the app binary regardless —
# committing them exposes nothing that the bundle does not already contain. The
# anon key is public by design; Supabase row-level security is the access
# control, not secrecy of this string. See "Keys" in CLAUDE.md.
#
# The reason they live here rather than only in CI configuration: Xcode Cloud
# clones the repo and runs ios/App/ci_scripts/ci_post_clone.sh, which needs both
# to build the bundled web assets. Depending on the Xcode Cloud workflow's
# Environment tab meant a build that had never been run failed on its first
# real archive with "Missing required environment variable". A committed default
# makes a fresh clone build correctly with no out-of-band setup.
#
# .env.local still wins over this file, so local overrides keep working.
#
# NEVER add SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY or any APNs credential here. Those are
# server-side only and must stay Edge Function secrets.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://tpjiqegneohtbcxapqnq.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6InRwamlxZWduZW9odGJjeGFwcW5xIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NzczNTg5MjUsImV4cCI6MjA5MjkzNDkyNX0.nfaaphL0IrLMMei9GuHlLTfCg5dPbg3gfnqIr3Sln1s
